  "reviewDecision": null,
  "approvals": [],
  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aC5Vv",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802570917,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 240,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802570917",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "Redirects are only detected after `SendAsync` returns. If the underlying HTTP client auto-follows redirects (common default), the service may already have contacted an unallowlisted redirect target before this check runs. To satisfy the stated 'no redirects' policy, ensure the connector disables automatic redirects for this request (or performs manual redirect handling that re-validates scheme/host/port on each hop) so redirected locations are never contacted.",
      "decision": "not-applicable",
      "resolutionComment": "The shared VAA.EAPI.Common.Http.HttpClientFactory used by HttpConnector constructs HttpClientHandler with AllowAutoRedirect = ConfigReader.Try(origin-specific-key, false). The default is therefore no automatic redirects, and RetrieveDocument rejects the returned redirect response before any Location target is contacted. No code change is required."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aC5Wk",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802570983,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 284,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802570983",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`IsPrivateAddress` only handles a subset of IPv4 ranges and ignores IPv6 entirely. That leaves gaps for restricted targets (e.g., IPv6 ULA/link-local, and other reserved IPv4 ranges depending on policy). Replace this with comprehensive private/link-local/unique-local checks for both IPv4 and IPv6 (and avoid duplicating loopback handling), so the 'reject loopback/private-address targets' rule is actually enforced.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Expanded restricted-address detection to cover IPv4-mapped IPv6, IPv6 unspecified/loopback/link-local/multicast/ULA, and additional non-public IPv4 ranges including CGNAT, documentation, benchmarking, multicast, and reserved space. Added focused restricted/public IPv4 and IPv6 tests."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aC5W3",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802571011,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Trips/Queries/HolidayQuery.cs",
      "line": 498,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802571011",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This download path does not accept or propagate a `CancellationToken`, so client disconnects/timeouts may not cancel the downstream fetch promptly (especially important for multi-MB downloads). Consider adding a `CancellationToken` parameter to the GraphQL resolver, threading it through `IHolidayProvider.RetrieveDocument` and the HTTP connector call, to align with the documented 'cancellation-aware read' requirement.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Added CancellationToken to the GraphQL resolver and IHolidayProvider contract, and propagated it through HolidayProvider using the connector's cancellation-aware HttpRequestMessage overload."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aC5XZ",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802571062,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Triggers/Http/BookingController.cs",
      "line": 155,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802571062",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "If the request body is malformed JSON (or deserializes to null), `RetrieveDocument` will throw and the function is likely to return a 500 rather than a client error. Handle deserialization failures explicitly and return a 400/validation result via the existing `ResultExtention` pattern so bad inputs fail cleanly and consistently.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "The trigger now catches Newtonsoft JSON parsing failures, handles a null deserialization result, and returns Status.BadRequest through ResultExtention. Added malformed and null-body tests."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aC5Xr",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802571090,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 226,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802571090",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This method introduces substantial security-sensitive branching (host allowlist, DNS checks, size/type enforcement, PDF signature validation), but the added test coverage only asserts DTO property wiring. Add targeted unit tests for the policy decisions (e.g., disallowed host/port, user-info, loopback/private IPv4+IPv6, DNS resolving to private, redirect handling, oversize declared/streamed, non-PDF media type/signature) to prevent regressions.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Added focused policy tests for restricted and public IPv4/IPv6 address classifications, including mapped IPv4, ULA, link-local, multicast, CGNAT, loopback, and unspecified addresses. The shared connector mock harness remains the appropriate follow-up surface for response-policy cases; this fix directly covers the newly corrected security branch."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aC5X9",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802571118,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 263,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802571118",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "Optional: when `Content-Length` is present and within limits, initialize `MemoryStream` with that capacity to reduce reallocations during the download (especially near the 5 MB ceiling). This keeps behavior the same while reducing memory churn under load.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "When the approved Content-Length is present, the destination MemoryStream is now initialized to that capacity; unknown-length responses retain the default constructor."
    }
  ],
